---
/**
 * The library, from the README's "Features › Library", checked against the app.
 * Mirroring: "Sync your likes" sends new likes to Spotify, YouTube Music and
 * Last.fm (LikeMirrorSection), and "Send plays to YouTube Music" adds finished
 * songs to YouTube Music's history (YouTubeHistorySyncSection); every toggle is
 * off by default. Nothing reports plays to Spotify (the optional "Auto-save
 * liked tracks" only saves often-played songs to Liked Songs). Flagging a wrong
 * match only marks it; the swap happens from the Sync tab (Resync, then approve).
 */
import FeatureRow from '../FeatureRow.astro';
---

<FeatureRow
  id="library"
  icon="library"
  overline="Your library"
  title="Spotify and YouTube Music, one library"
  screens={['library', 'playlists']}
  reverse
>
  <p>
    Liked songs, playlists, daily mixes and every Spotify mix worth syncing, from both services, in one
    library.
  </p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>
      <strong>Likes and history mirroring.</strong> New likes in Stash can be mirrored to Spotify, YouTube Music
      and Last.fm, and songs you finish can be added to your YouTube Music history. Each is off until you turn
      it on.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Wrong version? Swap it.</strong> Flag it from Now Playing, then pick the right one from the Sync
      tab.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Scrobbling, if you want it.</strong> Last.fm or ListenBrainz, off until you connect one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Recommended by Last.fm.</strong> Connect Last.fm and Stash keeps a rotating playlist of songs it
      suggests from your listening.
    </li>
  </ul>
</FeatureRow>
